From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: a loaded shell link keeps its ShowCommand (3709)

shell32: a loaded shell link keeps its ShowCommand

IPersistFile::Save wrote the link's window state (SW_SHOWMAXIMIZED,
SW_SHOWMINNOACTIVE) into the header but Load never read it back, so every
link loaded as a normal window and ShellExecute of a link ignored a
"maximized" or "minimized" setting. Load now restores it; any other value
stays the normal window.
---
diff --git a/dlls/shell32/shelllink.c b/dlls/shell32/shelllink.c
index 14d8ac7..22272c3 100644
--- a/dlls/shell32/shelllink.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shelllink.c
@@ -1079,6 +1079,11 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI IPersistStream_fnLoad(
 
     This->wHotKey = hdr.wHotKey;
     This->iIcoNdx = hdr.nIcon;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_SHOWCMD_NOLOAD
+    /* the header's ShowCommand; a zero (or anything else a link should not
+     * carry) is the normal window */
+    This->iShowCmd = (hdr.fStartup == SW_SHOWMAXIMIZED || hdr.fStartup == SW_SHOWMINNOACTIVE) ? hdr.fStartup : SW_SHOWNORMAL;
+#endif
     FileTimeToSystemTime (&hdr.CreationTime, &This->CreationTime);
     FileTimeToSystemTime (&hdr.AccessTime, &This->AccessTime);
     FileTimeToSystemTime (&hdr.WriteTime, &This->WriteTime);
